From 7036da48cf3758f70991a5b1068f4a859c315595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:29:51 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/3] sparc64: add runtime SPARC64 V CPU,
 MMU and SMP support

Recognize SPARC64 V and validate the PRIMEPOWER 250 firmware identity,
MMU modes and kernel TLB reservations. Reuse the Fujitsu physical TSB
and demap paths; validate secondary MIDs 0 and 1 before joining Linux.
Check supported MMU modes again after firmware returns.

Acknowledge degradation before enabling interrupts. Zero ECC status
retries; nested and unsupported errors stop with a locked-image record.
Corrected incoming data needs scrubbing and is not treated as recovered.

References: SPARC64 V Supplement R1.0 5.2.9, 5.2.12, F.1, F.10.1,
F.10.7, P.1.4, P.7.1/P.7.4 and R.3; JPS1 Commonality F.10.11 and
N.4.2/N.4.3. Huge pages and CPU hotplug remain unsupported.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
